      "description": "Watch Maritimo vs Casa Pia highlights and goals from Primeira Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. Maritimo and Casa Pia faced off in a highly anticipated Primeira Liga clash on August 8, 2026 . Both teams entered the field with a point to prove, setting the stage for a tactical battle in front of a passionate crowd. A Cautious Opening Half The first half was a disciplined tactical affair, characterized more by defensive structure than attacking flair. Casa Pia dominated the ball, maintaining 60% possession, yet they struggled to break through a resilient Maritimo backline. The visitors' best chance of the opening period came in the 34th minute when David Sousa rose highest to meet a cross, but his header was comfortably gathered by Alfonso Pastor . Despite the territorial advantage for the away side, the teams headed into the break with the deadlock unbroken. Guzzo Makes the Breakthrough The momentum shifted in the 61st minute as the home side found their clinical edge. A well-crafted move saw Martin Tejon provide a pinpoint delivery into the box, where Raphael Guzzo timed his run perfectly to power a header home. The stadium erupted as Maritimo took the lead against the run of play. Casa Pia attempted to respond immediately, forcing several corners through Rochinha , but the deliveries failed to find a teammate in the crowded penalty area. Holding Firm Under Late Pressure As the match entered its final stages, the atmosphere grew increasingly tense, leading to a flurry of tactical substitutions and bookings. Maritimo 's Raphael Guzzo and Tomas Tavares both saw yellow cards during a frantic stoppage time, while Alassana Jatta was cautioned for the visitors. Despite a late surge from Casa Pia , including a long-range effort from Henrique Araujo that was safely handled by Alfonso Pastor , the home side held firm to secure all three points in a gritty professional performance."
